# core v3.10 — POSITIVE. A social history record carrying a consent scope.
#
# core v3.10 declares cascade:consentScope, the property whose only value --
# cascade:SocialHistoryConsent -- had existed since core v3.0 with nothing to
# carry it and nothing to check it. cascade:ConsentScopeShape is the first
# constraint in this specification that mentions consent, and before this
# fixture pair it shipped with zero constraint executions behind it: a record
# carrying a consent scope that was absent, wrong or invented validated
# identically.
#
# WHY A SOCIAL HISTORY RECORD. clinical.ttl states on clinical:SocialHistoryRecord
# that the class "requires separate consent scope (cascade:SocialHistoryConsent)",
# so this is the record type the property was defined for, and the one a producer
# will write it on first.
#
# WHAT MUST NOT BE READ INTO THIS FIXTURE. It does not assert that a social
# history record needs a consent scope. Nothing in core v3.10 requires the
# property anywhere, at any severity: cascade:ConsentScopeShape is
# sh:targetSubjectsOf, so it constrains the VALUE wherever the predicate appears
# and reports nothing on a record that omits it. That half is asserted by
# social-history-smoking.ttl, which carries no consent scope, is deliberately
# left unedited, and still passes. This fixture is the other half: given the
# predicate, the value is checked.
#
# Everything else here mirrors social-history-smoking.ttl, so the pair differs
# in exactly one respect -- the value of cascade:consentScope -- and the
# INVALID sibling isolates the sh:in constraint.
#
# Fully synthetic.

@prefix cascade: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/core/v1#> .
@prefix clinical: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/clinical/v1#> .
@prefix health: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/health/v1#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<urn:cascade:social-history:example-consent-scope>
    a clinical:SocialHistoryRecord ;
    clinical:socialHistoryCategory "smokingStatus" ;
    health:smokingStatus "never" ;
    cascade:consentScope cascade:SocialHistoryConsent ;
    cascade:dataProvenance cascade:EHRVerified .
